<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32165" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ocrĭcŭlum</span></b> , i,
			n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in Umbria</i>, the mod. <i>Otricoli</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				22, 11, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 6, 25, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. H. 3,
			78</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ocrĭcŭ-lānus</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ocrĭcŏlānus</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Otrĭ-cŭlānus</span></b> ), a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Ocriculum</i>, <i>Ocriculan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ocriculana villa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Mil. 24, 64</span></i>
			.—The tribus OCRIC., <i><span class="en">Inscr.
				Grut. 189, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">194, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1031,
			4</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. II. p.
			16</span></i>.—In <i>plur. subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ocrĭcŭlāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Ocriculum</i>, <i>the
				Ocriculans</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 9, 41</span></i>.</div>
